    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**1. Fixed missing named exports in `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`:**\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - These constants were being imported from `schema.js` but weren't being re-exported, causing the governance test to fail when trying to use `APPROVAL_STATUSES.join(', ')`\n\n**2. Fixed toxicity metric evaluation in `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`:**\n   - Changed `DEFAULT_METRICS` to wrap `toxicityMetric` so it only receives the outputs parameter\n   - Previously, when `runEvaluations` called it with `(outputs, references)`, the references were being treated as banned terms, causing all outputs to be flagged as toxic\n   - Now the function correctly uses its default banned terms for the toxicity check\n\nAll 28 tests in the frai-core test suite now pass, and all public exports remain intact.",
